Z||000003||Tom88gt||12-21-2000||10:44 PM||||Sorry dude but the sound your describing sounds like your engine has had an internal failure and is in the process of self destructing.  Loud banging from inside the engine is something loose or broken and slinging around.  <P>1.  A bent/broken rod will bang around a lot, have low power, and a damaged bearing (souce of oil pressure loss).  New engine needed.  <P>2.  A bent/thrown push rod may cause  the loud banging under the valve cover.  The lifter may have exited its bore, also causing loss of oil pressure.  Possible to fix engine while still in car.<P>I am giving you the worst case senarios and without actually seeing the car I can only give you some ideas.  Seek professional help.||||reg||1
