Z||000013||Fformula88||12-23-2000||11:23 AM||||If it was as loud as you described... sounds like its going to be fairly bad. To get a re-engineered engine from a shop installed probably run about $3000.  If the rest of your car is in good shape it may not be a bad way to go.  My dad got one of these engines in his 87 coupe, ran $2300.  So far he has 30,000 miles on the new one and it is still running great!<P>AS far as new cars with payments... they SUCK.  I am still paying for my 97 Probe and am very sick of cutting a check every month.  It may not need big repairs yet (knock on wood) but so far I have done brakes and tires and a tune up over the last year and it all adds up.  Plus parts for newer cars cost more than those for older cars.  I did a comparison between a few different "modern" cars and the Fiero, and the parts were all 25%-50% more expensive.  So as long as your Fiero isn't rotted out yet,  its probably more cost effective to repair than to buy new.  But thats just my 2 cents.<P>Good luck on your engine!  Hope its not anything too major!  This is a lousy time of year to need repairs.||||reg||1
