Z||000015||DavidHenshaw||12-23-2000||05:40 PM||||Advance auto sells remanufactured engines and I think I was quoted about $1200 for a 2.8 which includes the rebuilt block and heads. Of course anything you pay somewone to install it is extra. I believe a remanufactured 3.4 was in the $1600 to 1700 range. <P>A used motor is always the cheepest way to go. A used motor with some reasonable miles on it should be about $300 to $500.||||reg||1
Z||000016||StuGood||12-23-2000||05:59 PM||||Don't know how strapped you are for time, as I'm not in your situation, but if it were me, I'd start by checking compression.  If only one cylinder is down, it points to valvetrain trouble (punched rocker arm, bent pushrod, shattered lifter, etc.).  Might be able to repair it with engine in place.      ||||reg||3
Z||000017||Stoic||12-23-2000||06:24 PM||||Well, I can definately vouch for the condition of the car.  Very nice shape.  Worth the time and money, if you can spare both.  Good luck Scott.||||reg||6
